# Cursor entry point → AGENTS.md

`AGENTS.md` at the repo root is the single source of truth for every AI agent here.
This file adds no rules; it is a fallback for Cursor versions or modes that do not
auto-load `AGENTS.md`.

1. If `AGENTS.md` is not already in your context (current Cursor loads it automatically),
   read it in full. If it is missing, STOP and tell the user — do not improvise.
2. Run its **Startup** section literally (one command, one receipt line), then follow
   it — Boundaries still apply in auto-run / YOLO terminal mode, and the task ends with
   the Completion tier.
3. On any conflict, `AGENTS.md` wins. If context was trimmed mid-session, re-run Startup.

Never copy or paraphrase `AGENTS.md` rules into any `.mdc` file (duplicates drift, then
conflict); never create a root `.cursorrules` (deprecated, ignored by Agent mode).
